\title{paweh: Power and Sample Size Analysis for Genetic Studies}
\description{
\code{paweh} provides prospective power and minimum sample size necessary (MSSN)
calculations for genetic and genomic association study design. Many standard
calculations use homogeneous, error-free assumptions. The package implements
published statistical-genetics methods for evaluating selected departures
from those assumptions, particularly locus heterogeneity and supported forms
of genotype and phenotype misclassification.
}
\section{Study-design families}{

The principal interfaces are \code{\link[=cc_power]{cc_power()}} and \code{\link[=cc_mssn]{cc_mssn()}} for case-control
designs; \code{\link[=tdt_power]{tdt_power()}} and \code{\link[=tdt_mssn]{tdt_mssn()}} for transmission disequilibrium test
designs with affected-child trios; and \code{\link[=qtl_anova_power]{qtl_anova_power()}},
\code{\link[=qtl_anova_mssn]{qtl_anova_mssn()}}, \code{\link[=qtl_threshold_chisq_power]{qtl_threshold_chisq_power()}},
\code{\link[=qtl_threshold_chisq_mssn]{qtl_threshold_chisq_mssn()}}, \code{\link[=qtl_multivariate_power_full]{qtl_multivariate_power_full()}}, and
\code{\link[=qtl_multivariate_mssn_full]{qtl_multivariate_mssn_full()}} for quantitative-trait designs. Calculations
are primarily parameter and model based and support prospective planning, not
downstream association testing.
}

\section{Visualization and interactive exploration}{

High-level plotting functions include \code{\link[=plot_cc_power]{plot_cc_power()}}, \code{\link[=plot_cc_mssn]{plot_cc_mssn()}},
\code{\link[=plot_tdt_power]{plot_tdt_power()}}, \code{\link[=plot_tdt_mssn]{plot_tdt_mssn()}}, and the quantitative-trait plotting
interfaces documented with the corresponding analysis functions.
\code{\link[=paweh_app]{paweh_app()}} returns an optional Shiny dashboard that uses the same canonical
calculations for interactive study-design exploration.
}

